# Google Teachable Machine

https://teachablemachine.withgoogle.com/ 

Google Teachable Machine is a free, web-based tool developed by Google that allows anyone to create Machine Learning models quickly without writing a single line of code. 
It is designed for beginners to visually understand the core machine learning workflow.

 Core Capabilities (What You Can Build)
The platform allows you to create three types of machine learning models using your computer's camera, microphone, or uploaded files:
Image Classification:
Recognizes objects, faces, or colors using a webcam or image uploads.
Audio Classification: 
Recognizes short sounds like clapping, whistling, or specific words.
Pose Detection: 
Tracks body movements and recognizes physical positions or gestures.
